synce-core (0.17-0~bookworm8) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in (serial_start_device): Wait for local IP
    to be assigned to the PPP interface before returning True, instead of
    returning as soon as pppd writes its pidfile. pppd writes the pidfile
    before running the connect script; signalling dccm at that point causes
    it to poll a non-existent address in a tight bind loop. The timeout for
    this second phase is controlled by SERIAL_PPP_IP_TIMEOUT (default 10s).
  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in: Add SERIAL_PPP_IP_TIMEOUT variable
    (default 10) to allow tuning the PPP link-up wait independently of the
    pidfile wait.

 -- Gustavo Perez Reyes <ghreyes71@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Mar 2026 02:00:00 -0300

synce-core (0.17-0~bookworm7) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in (serial_start_device): Call
    systemctl reset-failed on the transient unit name before invoking
    systemd-run; --collect cleans up the unit after exit but a unit
    still in loaded/failed state blocks creation of a new transient unit
    with the same name on reconnect.

