synce-core (0.17-0~bookworm6) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in (serial_start_device): Add --collect to
    systemd-run so the transient pppd unit is automatically garbage-collected
    after exit; without it, the unit remains in failed state and a subsequent
    connect attempt causes systemd-run to fail with exit code 1 because a
    unit with the same name already exists.
  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in (serial_start_device): Log systemd-run
    stderr output when it fails to ease future debugging.

 -- Gustavo Perez Reyes <ghreyes71@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Mar 2026 00:10:00 -0300

synce-core (0.17-0~bookworm5) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in: Add missing imports: signal, time.
    serial_start_device and serial_stop_device both use time.sleep() and
    signal.SIGTERM but the module never imported these; caused NameError
    on every serial connect, preventing signal_dccm_connect from running
    and causing the PDA to drop the PPP link (LCP terminated by peer).
  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in (serial_start_device): Suppress pppd
    stdout/stderr from systemd journal by adding StandardOutput=null and
    StandardError=null properties to systemd-run; pppd logs natively via
    syslog so systemd capturing its output caused every message to appear
    twice in syslog.

 -- Gustavo Perez Reyes <ghreyes71@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Mar 2026 23:50:00 -0300

synce-core (0.17-0~bookworm4) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in (serial_get_devnum): Fix Python 2→3
    regression: re.match.group(1) returns str; Python 2 allowed str < int
    comparisons but Python 3 does not. Convert to int explicitly; handle
    empty match group returning 0.
  * scripts/udev-synce-serial.in: Fix str+int concatenation: use
    str(devnum) when building linkname.
  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in (rndis_dhcp_config): Fix bytes/str
    regression: subprocess.communicate() returns bytes in Python 3;
    decode output before split() and string concatenation.

