synce-core (0.17-0~bookworm2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * scripts/synce-udev-serial.in: Replace background & with systemd-run
    --no-block so the Python event handler runs in its own transient
    systemd service unit, escaping the udev worker cgroup.  Since
    systemd >= 209 (Debian 8 / Ubuntu 16+) the "Cleanup idle workers"
    mechanism sends SIGKILL to every process in the udev cgroup once the
    worker becomes idle, killing long-lived children such as pppd.
  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in (serial_start_device): Wrap pppd with
    systemd-run --no-block --unit=synce-pppd-<linkname> so pppd runs as
    the main process of its own transient service unit with an independent
    cgroup that is never subject to udev cleanup.  Add the nodetach option
    to keep pppd in the foreground as the unit's main process.  Replace
    the communicate() wait (which relied on pppd forking to background)
    with a poll loop on /var/run/ppp-<linkname>.pid (30 s timeout).

 -- Gustavo Perez Reyes <ghreyes71@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Mar 2026 12:00:00 -0300

synce-core (0.17-0~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Port to Debian 12 Bookworm.
  * debian/control: Bump debhelper compat to 13, update Standards-Version
    to 4.6.2, remove Python 2 build-deps (python-pyrex has no Python 3
    equivalent for pyrapi2.pyx), drop libsynce-dbg (replaced by auto dbgsym),
    drop python-rapi2 (Python 2 only), drop synce-bluetooth (bluez-compat
    removed from Bookworm), drop synce-doc (non-critical), update Maintainer.
    Add python3 to Depends of synce-tools and synce-dccm.
  * debian/rules: Rewrite using dh sequencer. Add override_dh_makeshlibs
    to pin libsynce0 shlibs version to (>= 0.17-0~bookworm1) (tilde epoch
    sorts before release suffix in dpkg comparison). Add override_dh_install
    and override_dh_installman to rename p-binaries/manpages with synce-
    prefix. Disable Python and bluetooth via configure flags.
  * debian/compat: Removed; debhelper-compat in Build-Depends.
  * debian/*.install: Update library paths to multiarch layout.
  * debian/not-installed: New file; exclude libtool .la file from install.
  * debian/source/options: New file; extend-diff-ignore for autoreconf
    generated files (configure, aclocal.m4, ltmain.sh, Makefile.in, etc.).
  * configure.ac: Replace deprecated AC_PROG_LIBTOOL with LT_INIT.
    Add AC_CONFIG_MACRO_DIRS([m4]) so autoreconf finds custom m4 macros.
  * Makefile.am: Add ACLOCAL_AMFLAGS = -I m4.
  * scripts/synceconnector.py.in: Port to Python 3 (configparser,
    except-as syntax, updated shebang).
  * scripts/synce-serial.in: Port to Python 3 (configparser, print(),
    except-as syntax, updated shebang).
  * scripts/udev-synce-rndis.in: Port to Python 3 (key-in-dict syntax,
    updated shebang).
  * scripts/udev-synce-serial.in: Port to Python 3 (configparser,
    key-in-dict syntax, except-as syntax, updated shebang).
  * dccm/synce-unlock: Port to Python 3 (print(), input(), updated shebang).
  * etc/org.synce.dccm.conf: Remove overly broad D-Bus policy rule
    (<allow send_type="method_call"/>); specific send_destination rules
    are sufficient.

